      "math_academy_id": "q-50036",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "A train is moving north-east with velocity $v(t)=6{t}^{2}+8t+100\\,\\text{km/h},$ where $t$ is the time in hours. Find the average velocity of the train on the interval $t\\in [1,4].$",
      "worked_solution": "To calculate the average value of the velocity on $[{t}_{1},{t}_{2}],$ we use the average value formula\n\n$$\n{v}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}}{\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{4-1}\\,{\\int }_{1}^{4}(6{t}^{2}+8t+100)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(2{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}+100t){|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}((2(4)^{3}+4(4)^{2}+100(4))-(2(1)^{3}+4(1)^{2}+100(1))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}((128+64+400)-(2+4+100)) \\\\  & =162.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average velocity is $162\\,\\text{km/h}.$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
